  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Velvet Noir — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Velvet Noir.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Velvet Noir.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Velvet Noir"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Velvet Noir" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #14030C   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #F6E4DA   crema     — primary text (16.25:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #36AFAB   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #14030C   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #3A1528   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #F6E4DA   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #F6E4DA   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #D4445E   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #1F0514   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #36AFAB   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #1F0514   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #D4445E   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #51A460   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #E28233   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #6486B9   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #C85BA0   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #36AFAB   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #E3CAC0   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #A88594   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #EC6175   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #70BB7C   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #E8A72D   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #7B9ED2   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #E076B7   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #59CAC5   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #36AFAB;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #F6E4DA   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
